Glad you like it. We're doing our best to carry the spirit over to the
target language. I still think we owe the game a few puns, though. We
lose things like "pit viper" -- I forget what that snake is called
exactly, but there's nothing about pits in the German name, and we had
to drop some funny messages that weren't funny in German. So where we
get a chance, we put a new pun or two in.

You'd also appreciate our Entweihwasser: "holy water" in German is
Weihwasser, literally either "consecrated water" or "water for
consecrating", and so it was natural to translate "unholy water" as
"Entweihwasser", a neologism that can only be understood as meaning
"desecrating water".

Want more? Learn German, play the game. Oh -- my partner Karlo has
explained some of his naming choices on the website too: www.netzhack.org/w=
arum.html
